 "gossip": {
  "text": "Zay Flowers is doubtful for Sunday after aggravating that left hamstring and missing most of the week's practices. Nnamdi Madubuike is out with a neck injury, and T.J. Tampa joined the out list this morning with a knee. Trey Hendrickson is now questionable with a finger, of all things. So naturally the Ravens have gone from 7.5-point favourites over New Orleans to 8.5, and their title price has shortened from +920 to +900. My read is that the market is telling you what it thinks of the Saints, not that it missed Flowers limping. Rob and Darren, you share this team across four bets and you're favoured in all four. Enjoy it, but my hunch is that a roster shedding bodies at this rate sends the bill in January. They're wearing all white on Sunday. Matches the bandages.\n\nNow, my medicine. Yesterday I said, loudly, that 52% for Rob over Darren's Bengals looked stingy, and I was leaning on Joe Burrow's questionable back. Burrow then practised in full on Friday and is set to start in Houston. Darren, that one's yours. Rob, I've been shouting on your behalf with no ammunition. Cincinnati is still a 2.5-point underdog and I still prefer the Chiefs, but it's a coin flip and I'll call it one.\n\nAndy, the only Lions news is the title price drifting from +1900 to +2000. No fresh names on the injury list. The market just thought about Detroit a bit longer. Steve, nothing happened to you. Again.",
  "written": "2026-09-19T06:16:18-07:00",
  "based_on": 23
 }
}